{
  "id": "perturbation",
  "term": "perturbation",
  "definition": "In this context, a perturbation is an imposed change in sensory feedback during speech, such as a shift in the heard sound of one’s own voice. It disrupts normal speech control and prompts partial compensation and short-term sensorimotor learning, with some aftereffects persisting when the change is removed.",
